ng to read while I hop on Line 2 from Sinchon ahahahahah</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh coolio, another Korean. Granted, I was born in the States and lived there until 2nd grade but I've spent the rest of my life in Seoul.<br /> <br /> And yeah, added a few Korean things here and there. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> Edit: Hang on, now I remember why that username seemed familiar - I've checked your Legacy updates before joining the forum proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27777-danielxcutter","name":"danielxcutter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T08:01:37-08:00","id":1501868,"title":"","content":"pretty impressive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T08:08:39-08:00","id":1501869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501862-homebrew-seoul-contagion-of-causality?p=1501868#post1501868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">pretty impressive</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Put in a lot of thought and effort into this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27777-danielxcutter","name":"danielxcutter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T12:34:16-08:00","id":1501898,"title":"","content":"I have only the one thing to contribute beyond my appreciation for the work and it's quality, and that is my feeble attempt to campaign that the name of the ghost of Death Wolf should simply be Sheut Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T15:32:36-08:00","id":1501904,"title":"","content":"Still reading, but can I ask what the significance of the Shadow Name Douksini is? My search engine skills are lackluster","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T18:25:47-08:00","id":1501910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501862-homebrew-seoul-contagion-of-causality?p=1501904#post1501904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still reading, but can I ask what the significance of the Shadow Name Douksini is? My search engine skills are lackluster</div> </div> </div> </div>\ub450\uc5b5\uc2dc\ub2c8<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the name of a famed-among-the-obscure supernatural creature in Korean folklore. Exactly <b>what </b>it is supposed to be, though, varies significantly depending on which literary source you\u2019re consulting (and which work of fiction makes use of them). Commonly, the word refers to a brutish creature much like the Japanese Oni, or the Korean-Buddhist Yacha and Nachal (derived from the Hindu Yaksha and Rakshasa respectively).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T19:15:15-08:00","id":1501912,"title":"","content":"So kinda like a bugbear (in the wider sense than D&amp;D) or boogeyman, at least in the level of variance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T19:54:08-08:00","id":1501915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501862-homebrew-seoul-contagion-of-causality?p=1501898#post1501898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have only the one thing to contribute beyond my appreciation for the work and it's quality, and that is my feeble attempt to campaign that the name of the ghost of Death Wolf should simply be Sheut Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHey, there are other candidates, like the Ghost of Death Wolf Past or Casper Wolf! XD<br /> \u200b<br /> Also thanks for the compliment! Did my best to emulate the official CC outbreaks, and from the reactions of people who read it it seems I've succeeded. :3<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501862-homebrew-seoul-contagion-of-causality?p=1501910#post1501910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \ub450\uc5b5\uc2dc\ub2c8<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the name of a famed-among-the-obscure supernatural creature in Korean folklore. Exactly <b>what </b>it is supposed to be, though, varies significantly depending on which literary source you\u2019re consulting (and which work of fiction makes use of them). Commonly, the word refers to a brutish creature much like the Japanese Oni, or the Korean-Buddhist Yacha and Nachal (derived from the Hindu Yaksha and Rakshasa respectively).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501862-homebrew-seoul-contagion-of-causality?p=1501912#post1501912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So kinda like a bugbear (in the wider sense than D&amp;D) or boogeyman, at least in the level of variance?</div> </div> </div> </div>A possibly apocryphal entity that in one source was described as bringing a &quot;plague&quot; to the people of the house Douksini visited - everyone who'd tried to kick it out, send it away, or kill it had their head smashed in after it left.<br /> <br /> Yeah, pretty good name for a Korean Obrimos Scelestus, ain't it?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27777-danielxcutter","name":"danielxcutter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T21:19:41-08:00","id":1501926,"title":"","content":"This RULES, OP! I'm definitely going to have to throw this at my players. I really just am thriving on the details here. I love this write up and it really does make me want to post my own contagion homebrew (Yellowstone: contagion of seasons / Renfeld County TN: contagion of the hunt) <br /> <br /> This is so so so good. I can't say it enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27762-jackal-alltrades","name":"Jackal Alltrades","avatar":"data:image