if you pay them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27777-danielxcutter","name":"danielxcutter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T20:35:50-08:00","id":1502280,"title":"","content":"Never thought of using Korea as a base for WoD games; I've used it in a Cyberpunk: 2020 game because I did, grow up, for a bit, in a Korean Immigrant-neighborhood; also, Vietnamese, Japanese, Mexican etc. In Cyberpunk, it was home to a totalitarian-government, based off of Orwell's 1984.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T22:30:16-08:00","id":1502283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1501862-homebrew-seoul-contagion-of-causality?p=1502280#post1502280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never thought of using Korea as a base for WoD games; I've used it in a Cyberpunk: 2020 game because I did, grow up, for a bit, in a Korean Immigrant-neighborhood; also, Vietnamese, Japanese, Mexican etc. In Cyberpunk, it was home to a totalitarian-government, based off of Orwell's 1984.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I didn't feel confident in my ability to portray other cities I've never even been to, and there'd have been too many to pick anyways. Whereas I've lived in Seoul for most of my life, so... yeah.<br /> <br /> Also, Korea or Korean people actually do come up occasionally, at least in 2e. I got Cheonsa from Night Horrors: Enemy Action (the Demon NH book), and another one from that book has a Korean lady as her secondary Cover. The 2e Promethean corebook has Seoul being unusually safe to make Unfleshed in (which I've also alluded to). The 2e Vamp ST Guide has Korea in the 1500s as a potential setting IIRC (this I didn't find a way to put in, but if I ever ended up running a game with this I might find a way to reflect that). But yeah, I guess it wouldn't be an obvious pick for most readers who don't live here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27777-danielxcutter","name":"danielxcutter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}